cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the SJSU18 secular-model dataset, please cite it as below, together with the
  papers whose recipe it reconstructs (references).
type: dataset
title: "SJSU18: a reconstructed degree-18 planar secular Hamiltonian of the Sun-Jupiter-Saturn-Uranus system"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: Armstrong
    given-names: Scott
    affiliation: "CNRS, Sorbonne Université, Courant Institute"
  - family-names: Komargodski
    given-names: Zohar
    affiliation: "Simons Center for Geometry and Physics, Stony Brook University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/scottnarmstrong/KAM-dev"
keywords:
  - celestial mechanics
  - secular Hamiltonian
  - planetary three-body problem
  - Sun-Jupiter-Saturn-Uranus
  - Poincare variables
  - Lie series
abstract: >-
  Machine-readable polynomial secular Hamiltonian (degree 18 in the secular Poincare
  variables) of the planar Sun-Jupiter-Saturn-Uranus system, regenerated from the recipe of
  Sansottera, Locatelli and Giorgilli (2013), with the generator scripts, the averaged
  reference semi-major axes, and validation tables against the published coefficients.
  Funded by the European Research Council (ERC), grant agreement No. 101200828.
references:
